From 056632dcd89afb35885deefabac768919e10cae9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sayzal28 <Sayzal28@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 14:19:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Open the brief form from a search suggestion's Generate
 button

Generate on a search suggestion card only showed "coming soon". It now
hands the card (title, the author's edited description and the four
sections) to the experiences page, which opens the New Experience brief
form filled in; the normal creation job and wizard follow from there.

- public-experience-chooser: an onGenerate host callback (the package
  cannot import app code, like Remix); without it the cards have no
  Generate button and say "Here are three ideas." The stub dialog is gone.
- composeSuggestionBrief puts the title and description first so the
  setup generator keeps them.
- Studio search page: Generate only for people who can author in the
  active project; it navigates to /studio/experiences?newBrief=...
- Experiences page: ?newBrief opens the brief form filled in (clamped to
  the 2000-character brief limit at a sentence end) and is removed from
  the address; a viewer gets no form and a console warning.

Checked on a local copy of the database: editor sees Generate and lands
on the filled form; viewer sees no Generate and the address is cleaned.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
